==Old English==

===Etymology===
{{PIE root|ang|dʰeyǵʰ}}
From {{m|ang|hlāf||bread}} + a second element representing {{der|ang|gem-pro|*daigijǭ||kneader}} (compare {{m|ang|dǣġe}}, {{m|ang|dāg||dough}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈl̥æːvˌdiːje/|lang=ang}}

===Noun===
{{ang-noun|head=hlǣfdīġe|f|hlǣfdīġan}}

# a [[lady]], the mistress of a household.

====Usage notes====
* As feminine equivalents of [[æþeling]], [[eorl]], and [[þeġen]] never developed, this was generally the title given to every noblewoman from the rank of [[baroness]] to [[princess]].

